events.full_message_head:
test: eval.js — align eval-var-leak expectations with strict-only engine

Two tests expected sloppy-mode eval var hoisting into the caller scope;
strict eval isolates declarations (ES2015 §18.2.1.3).

fix: map/filter ArraySpeciesCreate, CreateDataPropertyOrThrow undefined handling

- Array.prototype.map: use ArraySpeciesCreate instead of hardcoded ARRAY alloc;
  use array_set_elem_ulong_checked for

fix: eliminate all timeout tests — map length:Infinity RangeError + coll_construct IteratorClose

Array.prototype.map: add len > 2^32-1 RangeError guard before ArraySpeciesCreate so
{length: Infinity}

module: statement-level import() and self-import link guard

Statement dispatch peeks IMPORT before consuming, so import(...) as an
expression statement was routed to import_declaration and rejected;

private-fields: run base-class brand/field-init when invoked via super()

The SUPER_CALL path creates \`this\` for a BASE superclass itself but never
ran that class
